    {
      "id": "5bebe46cbcc5dee0517bfc4e5c1768008f7ca699",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2217009613,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Does this also work when using functions such as `min` and `max`?\n\nWould it be possible to use update `value_type_tostr` in `epan/dfilter/dfvm.c` to report the real return type? Right now it says `***`:\n\n```\n$ dftest --types 'max(tcp.srcport, tcp.dstport)'\nFilter:\n max(tcp.srcport, tcp.dstport)\n\nInstructions:\n 0000 READ_TREE        tcp.srcport <FT_UINT16> -> R1\n 0001 NO_OP\n 0002 STACK_PUSH       R1\n 0003 READ_TREE        tcp.dstport <FT_UINT16> -> R2\n 0004 NO_OP\n 0005 STACK_PUSH       R2\n 0006 CALL_FUNCTION    max(R1, R2) <***> -> R0\n 0007 STACK_POP        [2]\n 0008 IF_FALSE_GOTO    10\n 0009 NOT_ALL_ZERO     R0\n 0010 RETURN           R0\n```\n\nWould be great to have tests that could check that the return type properly got propagated :)",
          "author": {
            "id": 2415432,
            "username": "Lekensteyn",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Peter Wu",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/efcf30db53f30b15e7c905ef37bd4dc44d87573bd92baf97cd707115d3fcd0c0?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Lekensteyn"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-11-18T23:42:52.473Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-11-18T23:42:52.473Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 343587224,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 18124,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2320a116c04703eeea2cadcc2ac75dafe616436c",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2217014386,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Does this also work when using functions such as min and max?\n\nYes.\n\n> Would it be possible to use update value_type_tostr in epan/dfilter/dfvm.c to report the real return type? Right now it says ***:\n\nFor functions that always return the same type it works. However, some functions return the same type as their input parameters. For the variable return type functions it current lists \"***\".\n\nIt might be possible to update the debug output to list the expected return type.\n\nNote that there are some field abbreviations that have multiple \"compatible\" types registered, so the listed return value might depend on which field with the same abbreviation is registered last. They should all be numeric (in practice they aren't, which we should fix at some point. It's mostly ASN.1 dissectors that register fields that aren't compatible, I think one of the CI jobs lists them.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
